{"title":"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_(Super_Simple,_Easy,_&amp;_Intuitive)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution (Super Simple, Easy, &amp; Intuitive)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_(Bounds_and_Decimal_Part_Analysis,_Rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution (Bounds and Decimal Part Analysis, Rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Steven_Chen\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Steven Chen</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Mathematical_Dexterity\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There exists a unique positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for which the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b010978a55642b7f7aabb2df2f7cf45c9db937a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[U=\\sum_{n=1}^{2023}\\left\\lfloor\\dfrac{n^{2}-na}{5}\\right\\rfloor\\]\" width=\"148\" height=\"50\" /> is an integer strictly between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d51ea422092ef90627083ec6fe2db733d1038957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. For that unique <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f03b93d0a768b4232dd7cb3afcfd626a67a935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+U$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441416e660d25335f27e55334ac2a06e51541c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denotes the greatest integer that is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28Super_Simple.2C_Easy.2C_.26_Intuitive.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(Super_Simple,_Easy,_&amp;_Intuitive)\">Solution (Super Simple, Easy, &amp; Intuitive)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (Super Simple, Easy, &amp; Intuitive)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/724ec5377b0de7044d49ca4ee9ace22be0a0ed67.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\left\\lfloor x \\right\\rfloor + \\{x\\}\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />,\n\\begin{align*}\nU &amp;= \\sum_{n=1}^{2023}\\left\\lfloor\\frac{n^2-na}{5}\\right\\rfloor \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac15\\left(\\sum_{n=1}^{2023}n^2-a\\sum_{n=1}^{2023}n\\right) -\\sum_{n=1}^{2023}\\left\\{\\frac{n^2-na}{5}\\right\\} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{2023\\cdot2024}{10}(1349-a) -\\sum_{n=1}^{2023}\\left\\{\\frac{n^2-na}{5}\\right\\}.\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p><br />\nSince each fractional part is in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1a809324034256fb4541c3b1d336e005d488ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, the second sum is in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/4884925c16d2dc7af9fdd91f0bba091788c0a998.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,2023)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/44857633a8a9821323195189d04599857c29100f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U\\in(-1000,1000)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"20\" />, we must have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c707dbca15ab7e07e0bcab3f5be50af09894ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=1349,\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />\nwhich also proves uniqueness.\n</p><p>Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594c48b7ad59b4e07d0b72e2dd107be77f3834ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1349\\equiv4\\pmod5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c883ecf8bca75567efb62b923a5a5797dd8c6126.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2-1349n\\equiv n(n-4)\\pmod5.\\]\" width=\"264\" height=\"20\" />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090bf65257ffc94d6d125020fee81c8910eb008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\equiv0,1,2,3,4\\pmod5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"20\" />, the residues are\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40a8cc30b66b9e87e36246b20793d45f1454340c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0,2,1,2,0.\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />\nHence the corresponding fractional parts are\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16e0edf6b124babf93c540d02cf8e60d74b4ddc8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0,\\frac25,\\frac15,\\frac25,0,\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"37\" />\nwhose sum over each block of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/7/b971bfa1a7ad3bc59294e963acda7e86b454b3bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2023=5(404)+3,\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />\nthe first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509a9369d5c55fd98dc99cb2938fb44f0101f90a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> terms contribute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c966a8bbbfff128d433f2021f9993ed52e87fcbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$404$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, while the remaining three contribute\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3eaac627e3ec89c5af0a47932fee77902df490cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac25+\\frac15+\\frac25=1.\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"37\" />\nTherefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/c/14c4fa6b12bc8de8b25fb53fa4bfe821fa67c61d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[U=-405,\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />\nand hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0baa84444206a3f1876a3f978389fcad669d7bad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{a+U=1349-405=944}.\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Puer_137\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28Bounds_and_Decimal_Part_Analysis.2C_Rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(Bounds_and_Decimal_Part_Analysis,_Rigorous)\">Solution (Bounds and Decimal Part Analysis, Rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (Bounds and Decimal Part Analysis, Rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec0a4f6cd6176fde653a3682023ee71375cd8802.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{ x \\right\\} = x - \\left\\lfloor x \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>First, we bound <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>We establish an upper bound of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />. We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae6bae8ccc73884d8378a22ad1c1e4c5387dd46a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} U &amp; \\leq \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{5} \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} n^2 - \\frac{a}{5} \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} n \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1012 \\cdot 2023}{5} \\left( 1349 - a \\right) \\\\ &amp; \\triangleq UB . \\end{align*}\" width=\"211\" height=\"178\" />\n</p><p>We establish a lower bound of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />. We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39e8a9e62c66f40a39d749b68a7b3103df7fb67.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} U &amp; =  \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} \\left(  \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} - \\left\\{ \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} \\right\\}  \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} - \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} \\left\\{ \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} \\right\\} \\\\ &amp; = UB -  \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} \\left\\{ \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} \\right\\} \\\\ &amp; \\geq UB -  \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} \\mathbf 1 \\left\\{ \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} \\notin \\Bbb Z \\right\\} . \\end{align*}\" width=\"273\" height=\"231\" />\n</p><p>We notice that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/1/941575d567ce342cc6af952add4bae65bcffd662.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 | n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/a/01ac2a42e9e40e60be2f8699a5f115eeff94ed64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n^2 - na}{5} \\in \\Bbb Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"101\" height=\"41\" />.\nThus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e25cf142c59a2be2f0d34fa670595ba5031c67bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} U &amp; \\geq UB -  \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} \\mathbf 1 \\left\\{ \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} \\notin \\Bbb Z \\right\\} \\\\ &amp; \\geq UB -  \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} \\mathbf 1 \\left\\{ 5 \\nmid n \\right\\} \\\\ &amp; = UB - \\left( 2023 - \\left\\lfloor \\frac{2023}{5} \\right\\rfloor \\right) \\\\ &amp; = UB - 1619 \\\\ &amp; \\triangleq LB . \\end{align*}\" width=\"255\" height=\"211\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/6/3d69d0228f1c384a3fbae13e0fd900ba8667c71c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U \\in \\left[ - 1000, 1000 \\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/8208314da919bcee9f8f822d06c93febf0fa10de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$UB - LB = 1619 &lt; \\left( 1000 - \\left( - 1000 \\right) \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"302\" height=\"20\" />, we must have either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/78814b78b3ea62fa4eeb10b75d59a3253eaef824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$UB \\in \\left[ - 1000, 1000 \\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/4/384dcdfeda8e260b2c0b1f0fd47e2c9b851e85b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LB \\in \\left[ - 1000, 1000 \\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/78814b78b3ea62fa4eeb10b75d59a3253eaef824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$UB \\in \\left[ - 1000, 1000 \\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" />, we get a unique <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8fe07a4e119e17ac85a5a77ab07794c2b1cc1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1349$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />.\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/4/384dcdfeda8e260b2c0b1f0fd47e2c9b851e85b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LB \\in \\left[ - 1000, 1000 \\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />, there is no feasible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8fe07a4e119e17ac85a5a77ab07794c2b1cc1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1349$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b031b665e708a43eb6ab74aa04d0395b46d5489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$UB = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/46873a0d37ccc7cf9b26e4ce2a1e545203456c83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 5 q + r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9151de39d7f8122c8bd7d4bd5149e6229a53295c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = {\\rm Rem} \\ \\left( n, 5 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d868d83628929be9e8881debf9014aaa6aff206.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left\\{ \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} \\right\\} &amp; = \\left\\{ \\frac{\\left( 5 q + r \\right)^2 - \\left( 5 q + r \\right)\\left( 1350 - 1 \\right)}{5} \\right\\} \\\\ &amp; = \\left\\{ 5 q^2 + 2 q r - \\left( 5 q + r \\right) 270 + q + \\frac{r^2 + r}{5}  \\right\\} \\\\ &amp; = \\left\\{\\frac{r^2 + r}{5}  \\right\\} \\\\ &amp; = \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{ll} 0 &amp; \\mbox{ if } r = 0, 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} &amp; \\mbox{ if } r = 1, 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5} &amp; \\mbox{ if } r = 2 \\end{array} \\right. . \\end{align*}\" width=\"432\" height=\"223\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1de45e898dc813bf8834eec25b40573baa1de36c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} U &amp; =  \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} \\left(  \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} - \\left\\{ \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} \\right\\}  \\right) \\\\ &amp; = UB - \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} \\left\\{ \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} \\right\\} \\\\ &amp; = - \\sum_{n=1}^{2023} \\left\\{ \\frac{n^2 - na}{5} \\right\\} \\\\ &amp; = - \\sum_{q=0}^{404} \\sum_{r=0}^4 \\left\\{\\frac{r^2 + r}{5}  \\right\\} + \\left\\{ \\frac{0^2 - 0 \\cdot a}{5} \\right\\} + \\left\\{ \\frac{2024^2 - 2024a}{5} \\right\\} \\\\ &amp; = - \\sum_{q=0}^{404} \\left( 0 + 0 + \\frac{2}{5} + \\frac{2}{5} + \\frac{1}{5} \\right) + 0 + 0 \\\\ &amp; = - 405 . \\end{align*}\" width=\"475\" height=\"318\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/731580cba7162845697163f4e8793d1ad35302b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + U = 1349 - 405 = \\boxed{\\textbf{944}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"222\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p><p>~minor edits by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Kevinchen_yay\">KevinChen_Yay</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2dd0eab0d6573a93aafe64a0c38bd82fc11e219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U&#39; = \\sum^{2023}_{n=1} {\\frac{n^2-na}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"140\" height=\"55\" />. Since for any real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c55bf81ec56326ec51563dafdf9c4ceedb6ed96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor \\le x \\le \\lfloor x \\rfloor + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"19\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b071cf6ed274a9907a70259c65b42425abbbfa19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U \\le U&#39; \\le U + 2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />. Now, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15cc3f1b7628ae980aac1ea50f13517ecdd8c45c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1000 \\le U \\le 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7ba17416e0317a8be57a18e8512a5b5c674505a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1000 \\le U&#39; \\le 3023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we can solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/6570aa6fb2420fa2b5432febc5ff9e33fc0e8e69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. We have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c282e79301cc245b07090dd8a063755120fc2dae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} U&#39; &amp;= \\sum^{2023}_{n=1} {\\frac{n^2-na}{5}} \\\\ &amp;= \\sum^{2023}_{n=1} {\\frac{n^2}{5} - \\frac{na}{5}} \\\\ &amp;= \\sum^{2023}_{n=1} {\\frac{n^2}{5}} - \\sum^{2023}_{n=1} {\\frac{na}{5}} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\sum^{2023}_{n=1} {{n^2}} - \\sum^{2023}_{n=1} {na}}{5} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\frac{2023(2023+1)(2023 \\cdot 2 + 1)}{6} - \\frac{a \\cdot 2023(2023+1)}{2} }{5} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{2023(2024)(4047-3a)}{30} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"310\" height=\"316\" />\nSo, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec3042c4667fdd65e3b85a9619af64a7fefde07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U&#39; = \\frac{2023(2024)(4047-3a)}{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"227\" height=\"40\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7ba17416e0317a8be57a18e8512a5b5c674505a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1000 \\le U&#39; \\le 3023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af432b63382140bcfee04c729256ae3aec1db5a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1000 \\le \\frac{2023(2024)(4047-3a)}{30} \\le 3023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"319\" height=\"40\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8ebed5620645b8d67e30e76bd8e8862790f8c521.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-30000 \\le 2023(2024)(4047-3a) \\le 90690$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"334\" height=\"20\" />. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a788acf7ba2350c4914b0fd311a6f78f92259ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023 \\cdot 2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" /> is much bigger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/f/06fe351f7df5b9279632b4508ce9a9996d368ab1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90690$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b1e77536dfe4ca5484fa053116b8f1a10034500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30000$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c8297a614626ad3a7e00ad08359e796e26de6c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4047-3a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" /> is an integer, to satsify the inequalities, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7637fbb1fafe0c814bf56e5bbcb5d23cbf5b5943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4047 - 3a = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8fe07a4e119e17ac85a5a77ab07794c2b1cc1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1349$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d083a2fe219d2d7d863a57c3939640e92feda8e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U&#39; = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f641eab1887864d45bbef71922d91be278afa7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U - U&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" />. We have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a208578596aaeb80b58b952a968c6c5122a61dc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} U - U&#39; &amp;= \\sum^{2023}_{n=1} {\\lfloor \\frac{n^2-1349n}{5} \\rfloor} - \\sum^{2023}_{n=1} {\\frac{n^2-1349n}{5}} \\\\ &amp;= \\sum^{2023}_{n=1} {\\lfloor \\frac{n^2-1349n}{5} \\rfloor - \\frac{n^2-1349n}{5}} \\end{align*}.\" width=\"447\" height=\"132\" />\nNow, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/6024dd4366e0f4d17739321b773a24c8cfbf2c4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-1349n \\equiv 0 \\text{ (mod 5)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"21\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/62200ea1308a9327bf416e01869347589bfe7c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\frac{n^2-1349n}{5} \\rfloor - \\frac{n^2-1349n}{5} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"257\" height=\"41\" />, and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/5/6051983e93cbd90de628fb010d0d2b6a2f5778d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-1349n \\equiv 1 \\text{ (mod 5)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"21\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6ed0c27e8c678daa6cd9f6d00982e312b113a068.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\frac{n^2-1349n}{5} \\rfloor - \\frac{n^2-1349n}{5} = -\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"275\" height=\"41\" />, and so on. Testing with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/f/dffb981ed4295f44ef700b2f54415a9ea21b1aa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 0,1,2,3,4, \\text{ (mod 5)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07b985cc40d1fc0c5b6a47cee826759a47f290b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-1349n \\equiv 0,2,1,2,0 \\text{ (mod 5)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"256\" height=\"21\" /> respectively. From 1 to 2023, there are 405 numbers congruent to 1 mod 5, 405 numbers congruent to 2 mod 5, 405 numbers congruent to 3 mod 5, 404 numbers congruent to 4 mod 5, and 404 numbers congruent to 0 mod 5. So, solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f641eab1887864d45bbef71922d91be278afa7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U - U&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" />, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e9f3c9b743fe8384ffc8429d3c014ad19eecba2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} U - U&#39; &amp;= \\sum^{2023}_{n=1} {\\lfloor \\frac{n^2-1349n}{5} \\rfloor - \\frac{n^2-1349n}{5}} \\\\ &amp;= 404 \\cdot 0 - 405 \\cdot \\frac{2}{5} - 405 \\cdot \\frac{1}{5} - 405 \\cdot \\frac{2}{5} - 404 \\cdot 0 \\\\ &amp;= -405(\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\ &amp;= -405 \\end{align*}\" width=\"426\" height=\"159\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d083a2fe219d2d7d863a57c3939640e92feda8e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U&#39; = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" />, this gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/5/cd5ad92a6c9c96a98eb6fba99c986cca5d76b365.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U = -405$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />, and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b6c8d80112c256ddb4e102e120cd66c57d164d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + U = 1349-405 = \\boxed{944}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"221\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ genius_007\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Quick)\">Solution 3 (Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can view the floor function in this problem as simply subtracting the remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036ab63f3e3b3f0a3134e74874835ba2be2fdaa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 - na$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> (mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) from the numerator of  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/5302ea7332f3214fd3d618f7b84705c067d71129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n^2-na}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"41\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2c25b9e66a08b60d180d90d16c6be2bd5d82e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{7}{5} \\right\\rfloor = \\frac{7-2}{5} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"138\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Note that the congruence of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036ab63f3e3b3f0a3134e74874835ba2be2fdaa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 - na$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> (mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) loops every time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> increases by 5. Also, note that the congruence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> (mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) determines the set of congruences of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036ab63f3e3b3f0a3134e74874835ba2be2fdaa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 - na$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> for each congruence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> (mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). \n</p><p>For example, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b39e2dc89f7b1582d29175748fcaa817a9b67b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\equiv 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> (mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), the set of remainders is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b2825169b304ff286a4bdef81850d9384aa45bfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 2, 1, 2, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/270b9887623abcb08f406a72bba869acc41a0131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 1,2,3,4,0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"17\" /> (mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). Let the sum of these elements be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Note that for each “loop” of the numerator (mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), each element of the set will be subtracted exactly once, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is subtracted once for each loop. The value of the numerator will loop <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c966a8bbbfff128d433f2021f9993ed52e87fcbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$404$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> times (mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) throughout the sum, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/1/3f17dd8b5aa572eca1964dd78f4d2c699b49b5b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 404=2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" />. Then \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b60501bd2ecbd3c033328004d83bc694eeb8979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U \\approx \\frac {\\left( \\frac {n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6} - \\frac{(a)(n)(n+1)}{2}  -404s \\right)}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"311\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aea1006b26d408cefb24029ea6e7af35496013a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. Note that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/1/3f17dd8b5aa572eca1964dd78f4d2c699b49b5b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 404=2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" />, this is an approximation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> because the equation disregards the remainder (mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6b1a2a2d813e9439df81e73bfc18778d9cab12c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2021, 2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> so we must subtract the first 3 terms of our set of congruences one extra time to get the exact value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> (*). However, we will find that this is a negligible error when it comes to the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c57effc77e6833a8f871109f084319afc72988d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1000&lt;U&lt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"16\" />, so we can proceed with this approximation to solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>Factoring our approximation gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a760a63c697008e22a45edb3cc5f8e8f9593b5ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U \\approx \\frac {\\frac{(n)(n+1)(2n+1 - 3a)}{6}-404s}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"227\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWe set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75bd79e1671a028e9c56433cb7879bdd67a099c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a= \\frac{(2n+1)}{3} = 1349$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"40\" /> to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93bfa3f50a3c2d30d17992ac7669b6e719b984c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(n)(n+1)(2n+1 - 3a)}{6}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"227\" height=\"40\" />, accordingly minimizing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94dbd2fa8401ca710a649d6bb8152217f14873c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|U|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" />, yielding  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1e0b652bd0f2f883e62216cf042327b323c3d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U \\approx  \\frac{-404s}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> increases or decreases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> changes by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82c5be1d08d8e4aef41f4d43ccd92a278b86da5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {(n)(n+1)}{2 \\cdot 5} = \\frac {2023 \\cdot 2024}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"201\" height=\"40\" />\nwhich clearly breaks the inequality on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/275aa3fe7ebbfbbc664bb0691a963601d872a6ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1349 \\equiv 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" /> (mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) giving the set of remainders <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/2/f529013704ffcba6d040ee32294b1356878ad2d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,1,2,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a29de43d66d80fe04c93e2a579f05540926bab29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and our approximation yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a53788d2bd4a00bcc183ff7173d4cbab0ddda168.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U \\approx -404$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />. However, we must subtract 2, 1, and 2 (*) giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e8f659d6dce863ce721a2e709c4691e7cfc48b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U = - 404 - \\frac{(2+1+2)}{5} = - 405$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"260\" height=\"40\" />, giving an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/552549ebc28082bd1d49e7e77c5e79adfc97e4cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1349-405= \\boxed{944}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"150\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Spencer Danese\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Calculus)\">Solution 4 (Calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the integral\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/4634fcf3cf4f098eb9dad9a55120b7a0b4fb2298.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\int_{0}^{2023} \\dfrac{n^2-na}{5} \\, dn.\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"44\" />\nWe hope this will give a good enough appoximation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45ef9cdc7c7d46920eac603663914e0d9261a99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> However, this integral can be easily evaluated to be\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/c/97cb2afa53e7e6dc2d378b374a6372f0c64c641e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{15}2023^3-\\dfrac{a}{10}2023^2=2023^2\\left(\\dfrac{2023}{15}-\\dfrac{a}{10}\\right).\\]\" width=\"340\" height=\"43\" />\nBecause we want this to be as close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as possible, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> should equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/e/cbe8b4cdfb314adf452f7f573e2856ad88cd96d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1349.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> Then, evaluating the sum becomes trivial. Set\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b3360ab46f8a1eb6e700b54c6cdc8a02c4d0d21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[U&#39;=\\sum_{n=1}^{2023}\\dfrac{n^2-1349n}{5}\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"50\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06da10ca389bb8982b124f504e1a7b127fadb896.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[U&#39;&#39;=\\sum_{n=1}^{2023}\\{\\dfrac{n^2-1349n}{5}\\}.\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"50\" />\nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a2a0f571c3f517f2f669a6c41c518e97c1b8558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U=U&#39;-U&#39;&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" /> We can evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/6570aa6fb2420fa2b5432febc5ff9e33fc0e8e69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/100137a219627a844894876ef58095c65ac742d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/d/30d620f9e4c22814d91fe9eb235e2660defec875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-405$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> (using some basic number theory). Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e31f1f1488eabf78104069f9f5cc1fa4f7bf8389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U=-405$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> and the answer is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/ddab0276ab61ee817c53b16464d02d71612ec31c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1349+(-405)=\\boxed{944}.\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"23\" />\n~BS2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tZSi6Ds9XgM?si=4RkUFtmr5rwKfyW6\">2023 AIME I #10</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://mathproblemsolvingskills.wordpress.com/\">MathProblemSolvingSkills.com</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jQVbNJr0tX8\">https://youtu.be/jQVbNJr0tX8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Steven_Chen\">Video Solution by Steven Chen</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Steven Chen\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fxsPmL6wuW4\">https://youtu.be/fxsPmL6wuW4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Mathematical_Dexterity\">Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class